# ---------- Uploaded content (never commit user data) ----------
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH ON PURPOSE.
#
# A bare `storage/` or `receipts/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, and git on Windows is case-insensitive by default. The unanchored form
# silently swallowed three real source directories --
# Application/Features/Receipts, Infrastructure/Storage and
# mobile/src/features/receipts -- so the code built locally, where the files sit
# on disk, and failed in Docker, which only ever sees what git tracks.
#
# Name the exact runtime directories instead. If the storage root moves, move
# the pattern with it rather than reaching for a wildcard.
/backend/ExpenseManagement.Api/storage/
/backend/ExpenseManagement.Api/uploads/
/backend/ExpenseManagement.Api/receipts/

# ---------- Logs ----------
logs/
*.log

